card F1, someone might take it for a pung. But since I have only one, and there are two left, it's possible. \n\nHmm. Maybe the best choice is to discard T4. Because the player across has already used it in a chow, so they might not need it. And T4 has 2 left in the wall. So it's less likely someone needs it. \n\nTherefore, I'll choose to discard T4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand contains a mix of Characters, Bamboo, and Wind tiles. Discarding T4 reduces potential chow opportunities while minimizing risk, as the player across has already used T4 in a meld.  \nReason: T4 is part of an existing chow in the player across's melds, reducing its utility. Discarding it avoids giving others a chance to complete new melds.  \nAnswer: Play T4"}
